  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Voluntary Contribution to Support IOM&apos;s Humanitarian Activities Supporting Internally Displaced Persons Living in Informal Sites</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian context in Iraq has evolved in the past years following the official end of the Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant (ISIL) crisis in December 2017. Since then, Iraq has been facing multiple overlapping crises resulting from the years of violent conflict, which have led to protracted displacement. Government dysfunction and lack of capacities to provide essential services has been compounded by recent regional tensions, economic hardship and political uncertainty, therefore heightening the country&apos;s fragility and risk of backsliding into conflict. The COVID-19 pandemic and its associated public health, socio-economic and mobility impacts have amplified these issues, often acting as a threat multiplier in Iraq&apos;s fragile context. Through this project, IOM is supporting the overall humanitarian response in Iraq. Specific interventions are based on existing and emerging gaps in IOM&apos;s humanitarian programme, and are focusing on the following sectors: Preparedness and Response in informal sites to improve access to basic services and safe, dignified living conditions, in line with humanitarian standards; Health in informal sites in informal sites to improve access to essential healthcare services; Humanitarian protection in informal sites to improve internally displaced persons (IDPs) access to strengthened protection environment.</narrative>
  </description>
